            <div xml:id="d904">

                <pb facs="0973" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hale</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1916-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                        1916</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is in receipt of a despatch,
                    dated November 20, 1916, from the American Vice Consul at Port Limon, Costa
                    Rica, which states that the Constitutional Congress of the Republic of <pb
                        facs="0974" n="872" xml:id="pg872"/> Costa Rica has granted to Doctor Leo J.
                    Greulich, of New York City, a concession for the privilege of exploring for and
                    exploiting petroleum and other hydro-carbonaceous substances in the Provinces of
                    Limon, Puntarenas, and Guanacaste.</p>
                <p>The Department desires that you investigate and report in full in regard to this
                    concession.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L.
                            Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
